# Proxmox safety

## Read-only default

List/get status/config/RRD are fine when Proxmox work is authorized. Do **not**:

- stop / shutdown / reboot / reset
- delete VM or LXC
- migrate / clone / resize disk
- change cloud-init or network in a way that drops management access

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the VMID (and node when
required).

## Sacred / deny-list guests

If the consuming repo defines sacred VMIDs or deny-lists (for example TrueNAS),
**never** power-cycle, migrate, or delete those guests — even when a broad
“fix Proxmox” ask is present. Say the deny reason and stop.

## Irreversible

Disk shrink, delete, and restore-from-backup onto a live guest: state the risk
and only proceed when clearly authorized (`global-execute-first` scope grill
for irreversible loss).
